{
  "_readme": "Golden canonical signing payloads. These bytes back every certification signature, so they are pinned here and read by the in-repo golden test, the netstandard2.0 parity probe (scripts/ns20-canonical-bytes-probe.sh) and the .NET 9 runtime probe (scripts/portability/net9-probe.sh) - one constant, three readers. To regenerate a case deliberately, copy the actual payload the failing test prints into this file. Regenerate ONLY when the canonical form is deliberately changed, and understand that changing it invalidates every signature already written. Doubles are emitted in ONE canonical form on every target - 17 significant digits on the invariant culture, both zeros collapsed onto 0, NaN and the infinities refused outright - because the decimal form a target's own formatter produces is not the same on all of them. CertificationRecordSigning.WriteNumberOrNull carries the reasoning; the awkward-double cases below pin the form, and they carry the values the targets measurably disagreed on before it was chosen.",
