    {
      "name": "v2-zero-signs",
      "why": "Negative zero. The record carries -0 for escapeRate and for one durationSeconds and +0 for the other; all three emit 0. The two zeros are collapsed onto one canonical form deliberately: a signed zero makes the writers agree and leaves the readers disagreeing, because the netstandard2.0 asset reads -0 back as +0 and would re-emit 0 from the same record file. Collapsing means this case also passes on a target whose reader never recovers the sign, which is what makes it the stable choice; -0.0 == 0.0 in IEEE-754, so no precision is given up.",
