    {
      "name": "v2-double-extremes",
      "why": "The ends of the range, and the case where a shortest-round-trip form and a 17-digit form are not the same text. escapeRate is double.Epsilon, the smallest subnormal, which any fixed-width decimal format destroys outright; durationSeconds carries 1e23, whose shortest round-tripping form is 1E+23 and whose 17-digit form is 9.9999999999999992E+22, and then double.MaxValue. Round-trip fidelity is what these pin: every value here re-parses to the identical bit pattern on every target.",
